      "writtenOn": "2026-09-10T02:10:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Neither one builds here. WEBP_BIDI_INDEXABLE and WEBP_INDEXABLE live in\nsrc/utils/bounds_safety.h, and this header only pulls in types.h.\n\nExposing them doesn\u0027t help either: WEBP_SUPPORT_FBOUNDS_SAFETY is set globally\n(CMakeLists.txt:427) while -fbounds-safety is per-target, and ptrcheck.h leaves\n__bidi_indexable undefined without the flag on purpose. With the swap,\nmuxinternal.c and muxedit.c both fail with \"expected \u0027;\u0027 at end of declaration\",\nsame for a TU including only mux.h. types.h:101 already draws that line.\n\nYou\u0027re right that it goes redundant long term, though. Drop the pragma and\n__sized_by_or_null deletes cleanly, I tried it. It just can\u0027t go first --\nmemcpy() won\u0027t take an __unsafe_indexable pointer.",
      "parentUuid": "a7ff292b_4fd86324",
